ds('not json') \u2014 raises ValueError (json.JSONDecodeError subclasses ValueError). Good.\n\nWhat about body='\"just a string\"'? json.loads('\"just a string\"') succeeds \u2192 JSON lexer. Not needed.\n\nNow, the module path: `httpie.output.formatters.colors`. Let me verify with get_info('get_lexer'). Also maybe get_info('httpie.output.formatters.colors.get_lexer')? The tool takes \"class, function or method name, as in 'f' for function f or 'C.foo' for method foo in class C.\" So probably just 'get_lexer'. Let me call it.\n\nAlso, I want to verify pygments lexer names/mimetypes available. get_info might not help for third-party. I'll rely on knowledge but make assertions robust: instead of asserting exact class equality via get_lexer_by_name (which is robust), that's fine.\n\nActually, one risk: `type(lexer) is _lexer_class('json')` \u2014 get_lexer_for_mimetype('application/json') returns JsonLexer instance; get_lexer_by_name('json') returns JsonLexer instance. Same class. Good.\n\nAnother risk: In some pygments versions, 'application/json' mimetype might map to JsonLexer only; yes.\n\nLet me also think about `test_mime_resolved_by_lexer_name` with 'foo/python': is there any lexer with mimetype 'foo/python'? No. Name 'python' \u2192 PythonLexer (pygments.lexers.python.PythonLexer). Good.\n\nHmm, wait: could `get_lexer_for_mimetype('foo/python')` accidentally match via the regex pattern quirk? Pattern `^\\*?(foo/python)$` matched against registered mimetypes \u2014 none is 'foo/python'. Good.\n\nNow, about cleanup: monkeypatch handles restoration automatically. No other state.\n\nAlso the instruction: \"Write as little top-level code as possible\" \u2014 just imports and test functions. No pytest.main.\n\nLet me also consider using pytest.mark.parametrize to reduce repetition, but explicit tests are clearer for coverage mapping. I'll write individual tests, maybe a couple parametrized.\n\nLet me now call get_info to verify the function and its module.\n\nI'll call:\n- get_info('get_lexer')\n\nMaybe also get_info('pygments.lexers.get_lexer_for_mimetype') and get_info('pygments.lexers.get_lexer_by_name') to confirm they exist as described. These are independent calls; I can batch them.\n\nAfter that, write the final test code.\n\nLet me draft the final test file:\n\n```python\nimport json\n\nimport pygments.lexers\nimport pytest\nfrom pygments.lexers.special import TextLexer\nfrom pygments.util import ClassNotFound\n\nfrom httpie.output.formatters.colors import get_lexer\n\n\ndef expected_lexer_class(name):\n    return type(pygments.lexers.get_lexer_by_name(name))\n\n\ndef test_mime_resolved_directly_by_mimetype():\n    lexer = get_lexer('text/html')\n    assert lexer is not None\n    assert type(lexer) is expected_lexer_class('html')\n\n\ndef test_mime_resolved_by_lexer_name_after_mimetype_failure():\n    lexer = get_lexer('foo/python')\n    assert lexer is not None\n    assert type(lexer) is expected_lexer_class('python')\n\n\ndef test_unknown_mime_returns_none():\n    assert get_lexer('foo/bar') is None\n\n\ndef test_plus_suffix_json_resolved_via_derived_mimetype(monkeypatch):\n    tried = []\n    real_get_lexer_for_mimetype = pygments.lexers.get_lexer_for_mimetype\n\n    def spy_get_lexer_for_mimetype(mimetype, **options):\n        tried.append(mimetype)\n        return real_get_lexer_for_mimetype(mimetype, **options)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(\n        pygments.lexers, 'get_lexer_for_mimetype', spy_get_lexer_for_mimetype\n    )\n\n    lexer = get_lexer('application/vnd.foo+json')\n\n    assert tried == [\n        'application/vnd.foo+json',\n        'application/vnd.foo',\n        'application/json',\n    ]\n    assert type(lexer) is expected_lexer_class('json')\n\n\ndef test_plus_suffix_non_json_resolved_via_derived_mimetype():\n    lexer = get_lexer('application/vnd.foo+xml')\n    assert lexer is not None\n    assert type(lexer) is expected_lexer_class('xml')\n\n\ndef test_plus_suffix_all_mimetypes_fail_falls_back_to