otation is loose in httpie. So my assertions should treat the return as an instance. `isinstance(lexer, TextLexer)` works for instances. And `type(lexer) is type(get_lexer_by_name('json'))` works.\n\nHmm wait, but httpie's own test does `assert get_lexer('text/plain') is TextLexer`? That would fail if it returns an instance... Let me think. In httpie colors.py:\n\n```python\ndef get_lexer(\n    mime: str,\n    explicit_json=False,\n    body=''\n) -> Optional[Type[Lexer]]:\n```\n\nand it returns `pygments.lexers.get_lexer_for_mimetype(mime_type)` which is an instance. So the annotation is wrong but whatever. My tests assert on instances. Good.\n\nActually hold on, let me reconsider: maybe httpie's get_lexer returns classes? `pygments.lexers.get_lexer_for_mimetype` \u2014 from pygments docs: \"Return a Lexer instance by mimetype.\" Yes, instance. OK.\n\nSo `isinstance(lexer, TextLexer)` \u2014 correct for the explicit_json condition in the code (`isinstance(lexer, TextLexer)`), consistent.\n\nNow finalize the test code. Also, I should double check the import path: `from httpie.output.formatters.colors import get_lexer`. Yes.\n\nLet me also handle the possibility that `pygments.lexers` isn't imported in the test module \u2014 I import it explicitly: `import pygments.lexers`. Good.\n\nLet me write the final version:\n\n```python\nimport pygments.lexers\nfrom pygments.lexers.special import TextLexer\n\nfrom httpie.output.formatters.colors import get_lexer\n\n\ndef expected_lexer_class(name):\n    return type(pygments.lexers.get_lexer_by_name(name))\n\n\ndef test_mime_resolved_directly_by_mimetype():\n    # Covers: candidate building without '+', mimetype loop with break.\n    lexer = get_lexer('text/html')\n    assert lexer is not None\n    assert type(lexer) is expected_lexer_class('html')\n\n\ndef test_mime_resolved_by_lexer_name_after_mimetype_failures():\n    # Covers: ClassNotFound handling in mimetype loop, for-else name loop.\n    lexer = get_lexer('foo/python')\n    assert lexer is not None\n    assert type(lexer) is expected_lexer_class('python')\n\n\ndef test_unresolvable_mime_returns_none():\n    # Covers: ClassNotFound handling in the name loop, None return.\n    assert get_lexer('foo/bar') is None\n\n\ndef test_plus_suffix_builds_derived_mimetype_candidates(monkeypatch):\n    # Covers: '+' branch building extra mime types; 'json' in subtype.\n    tried = []\n    real_get_lexer_for_mimetype = pygments.lexers.get_lexer_for_mimetype\n\n    def spy(mimetype, **options):\n        tried.append(mimetype)\n        return real_get_lexer_for_mimetype(mimetype, **options)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(pygments.lexers, 'get_lexer_for_mimetype', spy)\n\n    expected = expected_lexer_class('json')\n    lexer = get_lexer('application/vnd.foo+json')\n\n    assert tried == [\n        'application/vnd.foo+json',\n        'application/vnd.foo',\n        'application/json',\n    ]\n    assert type(lexer) is expected\n\n\ndef test_plus_suffix_without_json_resolves_via_derived_mimetype():\n    # Covers: '+' branch with 'json' not in subtype.\n    lexer = get_lexer('application/vnd.foo+xml')\n    assert lexer is not None\n    assert type(lexer) is expected_lexer_class('xml')\n\n\ndef test_plus_suffix_falls_back_to_name_candidates(monkeypatch):\n    # Covers: name loop trying subtype_name then subtype_suffix.\n    tried = []\n    real_get_lexer_by_name = pygments.lexers.get_lexer_by_name\n\n    def spy(name, **options):\n        tried.append(name)\n        return real_get_lexer_by_name(name, **options)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(pygments.lexers, 'get_lexer_by_name', spy)\n\n    expected = expected_lexer_class('python')\n    lexer = get_lexer('foo/bar+python')\n\n    assert tried == ['bar', 'python']\n    assert type(lexer) is expected\n\n\ndef test_json_in_subtype_appends_json_name_candidate(monkeypatch):\n    # Covers: 'json' appended to lexer names as a last resort.\n    tried = []\n    real_get_lexer_by_name = pygments.lexers.get_lexer_by_nam